---
description: Implement one evidence-backed Panestria R0-R3 slice at a time
alwaysApply: true
---
Read docs/PANESTRIA_PHASED_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md revision 3 and its active specification, then the selected AOS/extension slice and actual dependency code/evidence. Preserve unrelated changes.
Use one src/panestria distribution. Kernel owns task/approval/effect/budget state; UI/models cannot authorize or declare completion.
Use canonical verifier types, task_event, effect_digest, scoped identities and atomic datasource state/event transactions. External effects require intent/receipt/reconciliation.
Create meaningful tests for source requirement IDs. Record actual results; NOT_RUN/SKIP/UNKNOWN is not PASS. Mocks cannot certify required live adapter/hardware/OS boundaries.
Do not edit frozen references, weaken checks, introduce privilege bypass, provision credentials, publish/push/merge, or implement R4+ from a slice request. Live/account/OS provisioning needs its actual scoped authorization.
Read design files explicitly. This rule is coding guidance, not an OS sandbox or policy grant.
Continue to another ready slice only for an explicitly authorized multi-slice goal; otherwise stop after the selected slice. Report evidence, pending work and rollback. Expanded G3 requires 157 cases/trial/owner acceptance before separately authorized SOTA.

Use REA's investigation workflow for material reuse/recreation, with direct source inspection for complete repositories and artifact/runtime analysis when needed; retain pinned evidence, rights and integration tests. Quota uncertainty permits bounded work under policy, not invented balances or unapproved paid/training use. New profile/grant/phone boundaries require their registered conformance evidence before sensitive enablement.
